<title>USA: Old American in violation of covenants.</title>
<headline>Old American in violation of covenants.</headline>
<dateline>HOWE, Texas 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Old America Stores Inc said Friday it is not in compliance with certain financial covenants as a result of significant losses recorded in the first quarter.</p>
<p>The company said it is working with lenders to obtain waivers for the covenants and is initiating cost-cutting measures, including closing up to 25 of its 102 stores.</p>
<p>The company reported a net loss of $2.99 million, or $0.66 per share, for the first quarter, versus a profit of $119,000, or $0.03 per share, a year earlier.</p>
